From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: a popup that is a sheet of glass shows what is under it

0611 blends alpha-layered popups over what was under them as they are shown
(a virtual desktop's windows are children of its X window and X drops a
child's alpha). A popup that is a sheet of glass -- DwmExtendFrameIntoClientArea
with negative margins, or a swap chain with alpha (0605) -- has the same
black margins; it takes the same copy.
---
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -1620,9 +1620,12 @@
         if (data->embedded) set_xembed_flags( data, XEMBED_MAPPED );
         else
         {
-            /* an alpha-layered popup in a virtual desktop: what is under it, to blend over */
-            if (is_virtual_desktop() && data->layered && !data->managed && data->vis.depth == 32 &&
-                data->whole_window != root_window)
+            /* an alpha-layered popup in a virtual desktop, or a popup that is a
+             * sheet of glass (a swap chain with alpha: Chrome's bubbles):
+             * what is under it, to blend over */
+            if (is_virtual_desktop() && !data->managed && data->vis.depth == 32 &&
+                data->whole_window != root_window &&
+                (data->layered || (data->glass && (NtUserGetWindowLongW( data->hwnd, GWL_STYLE ) & (WS_POPUP | WS_CHILD)) == WS_POPUP)))
             {
                 POINT pt = virtual_screen_to_root( data->rects.visible.left, data->rects.visible.top );
                 take_window_backdrop( data->display, data->whole_window, pt.x, pt.y,
